  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current approach uses a multi-phased optimization strategy combining coordinate descent, SLSQP local search, and a repair mechanism. However, it struggles to escape local optima effectively. The proposed approach adopts a hybrid method that combines a global evolutionary strategy with a local coordinate-descent refinement. This allows escaping local optima through population-based exploration while leveraging a strong local optimizer on promising candidates.\n\nKey improvements:\n- Global exploration with an evolutionary strategy (ES) starting from the initial configuration\n- Local refinement using coordinate descent on best candidates\n- Adaptive parameter tuning for self-adaptation\n- Robust repair mechanism enforcing integral constraint\n- Timeout management ensuring timely termination\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nProblem representation:\n- n-point grid: h \u2208 [0,1]^n with \u2211h_i dx = 1 (dx=2/n)\n- Objective: minimize C_5 = max_lag \u2225h \u22c6 (1-h)\u2225_\u221e (linear correlation)\n\nAlgorithmic components:\na) Repair function:\n- Enforce 0\u2264h_i\u22641 and integral constraint\n- Handles constraint violations through adaptive clipping and balancing\n\nb) Evolutionary strategy:\n- Mixture formation: two-parent crossover with random mutations\n- Selection based on fitness (negative C_5 to minimize)\n- Uses repair mechanism for constraint handling\n\nc) Local adaptation module:\n- Gradient-based CD to refine candidates\n- Configurable hyperparameters with exponential decay\n- Success-based continued improvement\n\nd) Objective handling:\nC_5 computed via:\n  C_5 = |np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')| * (2/n)\nwith maximum over all shifts\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nPhase adaptation:\n- Global phase (60% budget) uses ES with crossover and repair\n- Local phase (40% budget) applies CD refinement\n- Fitness evaluation: repair(h) then eval_correlation(h)\n- Candidate repair using sliding window balancing\n\nMutation operations:\n- -Point mutations (0.05 probability)\n- -Two-point crossover (0.9 probability)\n- -Variable length changes (adaptive based on performance)\n\n CD refinement module:\n- -Single basins optimization using bi-section method\n- -Adaptive restart with scaled variables\n- -Strict integral constraint via repair function\n\nTerminal condition:\n- -Time-based stopping (600 seconds divider)\n- -Success threshold (moving average improvement)\n\n4. Search choices\nHyperparameter domain:\n- Population size: 20-50\n- Mutation rate: 0.05\n- Crossover rate: 0.9\n- Selection pressure: soft selection (\u03c3 adaptation)\n- Local adaptation steps: 100-500\n- Diminishing returns in temperature\n\nAdaptive heuristics:\n- Decision tree configuration based on fitness landscape\n- Success-dependent mutation intensity\n- Population triplex during stagnation\n- Temperature schedule: exponential decay\n\nUseful variations:\na) -Multi-resolution representation\n  Switch between low-resolution (n=100) and high-resolution (n=560)\n  Used during global exploration phase\n\nb) -Anti-robustness module\n  Introduce controlled fake violations to escape local minima\n  Adjusts during stagnation phases\n\nc) -Gradient sampling plus\n  Quadratic term in temperature schedule\n  Noise injection for enhanced exploration\n\n5. Budget estimate\n- Global phase: 600 seconds (ES operations)\n  - 20 candidates * 500 evaluations\n  - Repair operations: 600 repairs * O(n)\n- Local phase: 500 seconds (CD passes)\n  - 100 CD optimizations\n  - Fitness evaluations: 200\n- Total operations ~8e6 * (n\u00b2) computations\n\n6. Validation contract\n- Check feasibility at each step (integral, bounds)\n- Maintain finite values during optimization\n- Use repair to restore feasibility after repair operations\n- Final candidate repair and re-evaluation\n\nTermination criteria:\n- Time expiration (\u2264 1100 seconds)\n- Consecutive worst-case improvement stop\n- Restart triggers when improvement < 1e-5\n\nCandidates stored:\n- Best since initialization\n- Best since last restart\n- EMA-based termination\n\nComparison method:\n- New candidate repair and full C_5 evaluation\n- Compare against both best known and current best\n\nRepair recovery:\n- Sliding window balancing method\n- Random repair for historical candidates\n\nAdaptive restart conditions:\n- Performance plateau detection\n- Mixture parameter velocity limit\n- Fitness entropy threshold\n\nImplementation note:\nAll functions must use local repair to maintain feasibility.\nES operators work on integer [0-1] representation.\nTemperature schedule initialized to 1.0 with 0.985 decay factor.",
